From ec7dc261463bc09921ed4e22468c5d5eb35c1aba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:17:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: iris: fix clock unwind in iris_vpu_power_on_hw()

When enabling IRIS_BSE_HW_CLK fails, the error path jumped to
err_disable_bse_hw_clock, which disables the BSE clock that was never
enabled and then falls through to disable only IRIS_HW_CLK. The
IRIS_HW_AHB_CLK enabled in the previous step is left running, and each
failed power-on leaks one more enable count on it.

Jump to a new err_disable_hw_ahb_clock label that undoes the steps that
actually succeeded, in reverse order. Upstream main has the same
unwind.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XHbRyvZ53xawh6pBdmacMe
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
index cdb39f048..80c0681e5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
@@ -295,12 +295,12 @@ int iris_vpu_power_on_hw(struct iris_core *core)
 
 	ret = iris_prepare_enable_clock(core, IRIS_BSE_HW_CLK);
 	if (ret && ret != -ENOENT)
-		goto err_disable_bse_hw_clock;
+		goto err_disable_hw_ahb_clock;
 
 	return 0;
 
-err_disable_bse_hw_clock:
-	iris_disable_unprepare_clock(core, IRIS_BSE_HW_CLK);
+err_disable_hw_ahb_clock:
+	iris_disable_unprepare_clock(core, IRIS_HW_AHB_CLK);
 err_disable_hw_clock:
 	iris_disable_unprepare_clock(core, IRIS_HW_CLK);
 err_disable_power:
-- 
